/* book Worked example 2: Q: PWM uses fs = 10 kHz, τ0 = 50 µs and kw = 10 µs/V, with the leading edge at the start of each slot. Four samples are +2, +1, −1 and −3 V. Find each width, each trailing-edge time, and the shift of each PPM pulse made from those edges.
   1. Ts = 1/10 kHz = 100 µs, so the slots start at 0, 100, 200 and 300 µs.
   2. Widths τn = 50 + 10 mn µs: 50 + 20 = 70 µs, 50 + 10 = 60 µs, 50 − 10 = 40 µs, 50 − 30 = 20 µs.
   3. Trailing edges: 0 + 70 = 70 µs, 100 + 60 = 160 µs, 200 + 40 = 240 µs, 300 + 20 = 320 µs.
   4. Unmodulated edges would be at 50, 150, 250 and 350 µs, so the PPM shifts are +20, +10, −10 and −30 µs (kp = kw = 10 µs/V).
   5. Check the range: every width stays inside 0 to 100 µs, so no pulse merges with the next; the limit is |m| < 5 V.
   Answer: Widths 70, 60, 40, 20 µs; trailing edges at 70, 160, 240, 320 µs; PPM shifts +20, +10, −10, −30 µs, one pulse per 100 µs period. */
