/* book exam traps: PAM is not PCM: PAM is analog until it is quantized and coded. | PPM shifts a fixed-width pulse; PWM changes the width. PPM from PWM uses one edge per period, not both edges, which would double the pulse rate. | Duty cycle is τ/Ts (dimensionless), not τ·Ts. | The first null of a rectangular pulse of width τ is at 1/τ, not 1/(2τ). */
